## Context

Child of [[0870]] (integration review, 2026-09-29, author-approved). Commit
c9fe29db (ticket [[0878]], retirement of the legacy tables) deleted
`scripts/jetp/build_crs_comparators.py`,
`scripts/jetp/build_crs_energy_projection.py` and
`tests/test_jetp_comparators_crs.py` although they were not on the
retirement list: they are the only writers of the CRS comparator data of
[[0885]]. Nothing on main now regenerates `data/jetp/comparison/crs/*_Q.csv`
(80) + `manifest.csv`, `data/jetp/deflators.csv`, the 81
`line-fields/oecd-*` tables, `ontology/marker-coefficients.csv` nor the CRS
rows of lines.d (8,029), observations.d (40,145), timings.d (16,058),
relations.d (2,864), external-ids.d (10,514), documents (80) and retrievals
(80). `build_crs_bulk_sqlite.py` only writes a disposable SQLite.
`data/jetp/comparison/crs/README.md:9` still names the deleted script.

The integration review established, at c9fe29db^, that those builders
reproduce the committed data from pinned local inputs only (byte for byte
for the files, row for row for the sharded ledger tables). Restoring them is
therefore a reproducibility repair, not a port: the helpers they import
(`_ledger_headers.py`, `config/jetp-ledger.sql`, `catalog_crs.py`,
`build_comparators.py`) are unchanged since c9fe29db^.

Out of scope: `build_lines.py`, `build_evidence_layer.py`,
`build_m1a_lines.py` were one-time migrations and would change committed
data today; they stay retired. No new guard beyond the restored test.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The three files are restored from c9fe29db^ (`git show`, never
      `git checkout -- <path>`), with only the adaptations current main
      requires, each named in the PR
- [ ] On padme, from a clean clone with `data/jetp/crs` pulled and outbound
      HTTP pointed at a dead proxy, `build_crs_energy_projection.py` then
      `build_crs_comparators.py --recorded-at 2026-09-28` leave
      `git status --porcelain` empty; the CRS rows stripped from the ledger
      and rebuilt match the committed rows; one perturbed input digit is
      flagged (positive control)
- [ ] The restored test follows the repo convention: the test that reads the
      deposited ledger carries `@pytest.mark.slow`; `--collect-only` shows
      `check-fast` deselects it and `check-jetp` selects it
- [ ] `make lint`, `make check-fast`, `make check-jetp` (padme) pass
- [ ] `data/jetp/comparison/crs/README.md:9` names an existing script
